export anchor TheatrePlaybillStyle:
    number: 96
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Theatre playbill
    idea: The dashboard as an open theatre programme, two framed pages under a crimson valance, with the team as the company, projects as scenes in Act I, the fortnight as Act II and activity written as stage directions.
    base: light
    palette:
        programmeIvory: #fbf7ef, both pages, fields and the style sheet
        foyer: #efe7da, the table behind the open programme
        crimson: #8e1b2b, the valance, act labels, week two bars, Behind and overdue
        houseInk: #1c1a1f, text, rules and frames
        usherGrey: #4d4650, subtitles, roles and cues
        brass: #7a6328, ornaments, scene numbers, inner frames and week one bars
        lampGold: #e8c66a, the focus halo, never text
        laurel: #2d5a3a, On track
        amber: #83500a, At risk
    type:
        Titles and body use Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Libre
        Baskerville, Georgia, serif. Labels use Optima, Candara, Segoe UI,
        sans-serif in caps tracked 0.16 to 0.3em. The brand is 34px italic,
        the greeting 44px italic, act heads 28px small caps under a 12px
        caps act label, figures 30px italic, scene names 20px, stage
        directions 16px italic, labels 11 to 12px.
    layout:
        A crimson valance holds the italic brand, an outlined search field,
        the bell, an ivory New project button, the user in caps and a row of
        caps nav links, and ends in a scalloped swag edge. Below sits an open
        programme with a five to seven column split, a soft spine shadow
        where the pages meet, and each page framed by an ink line with a
        brass rule inside. The left page has the date kicker, the greeting,
        an ornamental rule, the overdue notice, Tonight's figures as four
        dotted leader lines with large italic numbers, and The company, the
        seven people in small caps with their projects in italic. The right
        page has Act I The projects with six scenes, each name joined to its
        percent by a dotted leader, meta, status and a thin brass bar, an
        ornament marked Interval, Act II The fortnight as a slim bar chart
        topped with diamonds, and Act III From the wings with each event as
        a stage direction starting Enter. Pages stack below 900px.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page margins, 32px between sections, everything on the page axis.
    density: Medium. Leader dots let names and values share long lines, as in a cast list.
    corners: Square pages and buttons. Only the valance hangs in soft scallops.
    borders: A 1px ink frame with a 3px brass rule 8px inside it on each page. Looped ornamental rules divide sections. Dotted leaders join names to values.
    shadows: Only the spine, a soft inner shadow where the pages meet, and a light lift under the spread.
    icons:
        Small solid emblems. A four pointed spark for On track, a half filled
        moon in a ring for At risk and a falling curtain triangle for Behind
        and overdue, each beside the caps word.
    focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px inside a 6px lamp gold halo. On the valance the outline is ivory.
    tone: Front of house voice, such as Tonight's figures, The company, Interval and Enter Sam Ortiz.
